[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit"]
[Variation "Queen's Gambit Accepted: Normal Variation, 5...Bb4+"]
[ECO "D26"]
[Character "positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "bishop-pair,central-pawns"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "5...Bb4+"]
[Start "accepted 4...e6 5.Bxc4"]

5... Bb4+ { Checks and pins the knight if it blocks on c3. } ( 5... Nc6 6. O-O Bd6 7. Nc3 { Develops and gets ready for e4, which would hit the knight on f6. } ) ( 5... Be7 6. O-O O-O 7. Qe2 { The same plan as in the main line: the queen guards the bishop on c4, the rook goes to d1 and e4 follows. } ) ( 5... Bd6 6. O-O O-O 7. Qc2 { Gets ready for e4, and keeps the queen out of the way of the bishop on d6. } ) 6. Nc3 { Blocks with a developing move. The pin does not hurt while White can castle next. } 6... O-O 7. O-O c5 ( 7... b6 8. a3 Bxc3 9. bxc3 ) 8. a3 { Asks the bishop. If it takes on c3, White gets the two bishops and the pawn on c3 holds d4. } 8... Bxc3 9. bxc3 { Plan: Qc2 or Qe2, then e4 to take the centre. The two bishops will like the open lines. } *
